import type { LevelSpec } from '../rules/types';

/**
 * The levels of the game: the row of the campaign after its prologue, the road. The row goes act
 * by act (`ACT_1`, ...), each act five to seven boards on one face or one pair of faces, with the
 * roles of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-vi-campaign-design.md, section 5.4; after the acts
 * comes the tail (`TAIL`), the list of the probe as it was, until the acts to come replace it.
 * The probe was a first batch made to find what a level of this game is.
 * Every level is a board to clear, given die by die: nothing comes to it. Only the faces a level
 * names work on it, and a die that has joined a combo goes in two moves. The floor is open and
 * strict: a die is rolled from on top and pushed from the floor, and the one way up is a die
 * that is leaving. A level is lost at a dead end: too few dice standing for a combo with nothing
 * going, or the player down on the floor with nothing to push and nothing to go up by, or with
 * too few faces that work. A level has no limit of moves: it is played as it is kept.
 * `progress.ts` rates a pass with stars.
 *
 * The list teaches nothing: no level says a rule or shows a move, and every level is open. What
 * a level is there for is not said here: a level is a place of `recipes.ts`, the place is a
 * form, and which is which is in the key, docs/VI_Levels_Probe_Key.md.
 *
 * The order is the owner's, of 12 October 2026: he played the probe blind and said of every
 * level where it belongs (docs/VI_Levels_Playtest_2026-10-12.md, section 4). A level keeps the
 * name it had in the probe, since stars and scores are saved by it, so the names do not go in
 * order. The levels of the probe that are not in the list are parked (`PARKED`); `P11` is gone.
 * `P31` was not in the probe: a breather laid for the list, after its hardest levels.
 *
 * The boards are not drawn by hand. They are picked by `node scripts/ladder.mjs place=P06` among
 * the boards laid by the recipe of each place: built from its route backwards (`route.ts`),
 * solved to the fewest moves, the route and the score of the way held against what the form
 * asks for, the parts of the route it leans on proved to have no way round. `seed` is the seed
 * the board was laid from, kept for the record: a level is its dice. `solution` is a way of
 * `par` moves, and the test of this list plays it.
 *
 * One level is not of its place: `P08` is a board of the road (`R10` of its second edition), and
 * the board its place was filled with is the piece `R08` of the road now, the two changed by the
 * word of the owner of 11 October. The reserve of `P08` is of its place still.
 *
 * The levels that were here before, the course and the chapters, are in the history: commit
 * 534b3ea.
 */
